From 26284cfdab5fc77ef470a5199f9dc21be249e113 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:30:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_expand: statics made while evaluating lifted statics name the crate

rustls 0.23.42 (xh 0.26.2), with 0285 past its match, died in Trans
Enumerate:

    <null> BUG: ASSERT FAIL: src/hir/hir.cpp:333:
    crate.m_ext_crates.count(path.crate_name()) > 0:
    Crate '' not loaded for ::lifted#C_76

HIR_Expand_StaticBorrowConstants_Expr (the on-demand pipeline that
constant evaluation runs on bodies it needs early) evaluates each
non-generic static it lifts. If that evaluation leaves a pointer to
an allocation it created, its Newval makes another static for it. That
static goes into the root module (m_new_values), but its path was
`HIR::SimplePath() + name`, with an empty crate name, unlike every other
Newval (and the lifter right above it, which uses crate.m_crate_name).
A lookup of the relocation in the same crate (Trans enumeration of the
literal that holds it) then asked for crate ''. After a reload from the
rlib it happened to work, because the loader puts the crate name into
empty ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_expand/static_borrow_constants.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hir_expand/static_borrow_constants.cpp b/src/hir_expand/static_borrow_constants.cpp
index 8ceb5fe8..b862aed9 100644
--- a/src/hir_expand/static_borrow_constants.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_expand/static_borrow_constants.cpp
@@ -1394,7 +1394,10 @@ void HIR_Expand_StaticBorrowConstants_Expr(const ::HIR::Crate& crate, const ::HI
             ::HIR::Path new_static(::HIR::TypeRef type, EncodedLiteral value) override {
                 auto name = RcString::new_interned( FMT("lifted#C_" << static_count) );
                 static_count ++;
-                auto path = HIR::SimplePath() + name;
+                // In the root module (m_new_values), so the path names this crate like the lifted statics above.
+                // `HIR::SimplePath() + name` (crate "") only resolved after a reload from the rlib (the loader puts
+                // the crate name in): rustls 0.23.42 "Crate '' not loaded for ::lifted#C_76" (Trans Enumerate)
+                auto path = ::HIR::SimplePath(crate.m_crate_name, {name});
                 auto new_static = HIR::Static(
                     HIR::Linkage(),
                     /*is_mut=*/false,
